Avenlet End User License Agreement (English translation)

Version: October 28, 2026. This translation is for reference only. If it differs from the Chinese version, the Chinese version prevails.

IMPORTANT: Please read this agreement carefully before installing or using Avenlet, especially the terms in bold that exclude or limit liability or restrict your rights. By installing, copying or using the Software you agree to this agreement. If you do not agree, do not install or use the Software.

1. Scope

1.1 This agreement is between you and xiaoxu123195, the rights holder of Avenlet (“we”), and covers installing, using and copying the Avenlet software (“the Software”) and related services such as software updates.

1.2 The Software is a preview release; its features may change between versions.

2. License

2.1 We grant you a free, non-exclusive, non-transferable license: individuals and organizations may install and use the Software on Windows computers, including for work, on any number of computers.

2.2 You may pass on our official installer unchanged. You may not modify the installer or the Software, distribute parts of it separately, bundle it with other software, or charge any fee for it.

2.3 The Software is currently free. The licensing of future versions, including whether they are paid, may change and is governed by the agreement shipped with that version. Versions you already have may still be used under the agreement shipped with them.

2.4 Third-party open-source components in the Software are licensed under their own licenses. See “Third-party notices” in the legal folder of the installation directory, also viewable under Settings › About. The restrictions in this agreement do not apply to those components.

3. Lawful use of devices and data

3.1 The Software can connect to phones, browse, collect and export data on them, and operate jailbroken iPhones and Android devices with debugging enabled. You may use these functions only on devices you own, or within the scope explicitly authorized by the device owner or the holder of the data, and you must comply with applicable laws, including the Cybersecurity Law, the Data Security Law and the Personal Information Protection Law of the People’s Republic of China.

3.2 You are responsible for making sure your use is lawful and for the data you obtain or process with the Software. You may not use it to obtain other people’s data unlawfully, to invade anyone’s privacy, or for any other unlawful purpose.

3.3 Jailbreaking, installing or starting TrollVNC, enabling USB debugging, using root privileges, and pushing or installing files on a device may affect its security, stability or warranty. You judge and bear these risks yourself.

4. Data and privacy

4.1 The Software processes data on your computer. It does not collect or upload your personal information, device data or usage, and it contains no usage statistics or crash reporting. Data you process with the Software is not sent to us.

4.2 The Software connects to the network only when:

(1) you send a request in HTTP Debugger;

(2) you use App Search to query app stores;

(3) you use AI features (AI Assistant, Translate, translation in the Quick Panel, and the AI organize, split into subtasks and summary features in To-do), which connect to the providers you configure in Settings › AI and to the network MCP servers you add;

(4) it checks for and downloads updates (see section 5);

(5) the installer downloads the WebView2 runtime from Microsoft because your computer lacks it.

In cases (1) to (3), data goes directly to the address you specify, the app store or the provider, not through us.

When you search the web or open a web address from the Quick Panel, the Software only opens the page in your default browser. The browser connects to the network, and what you search for is sent to the search engine you choose.

4.3 When you use AI features:

(1) What you type, the files and images you attach, and, once you turn on Tools, the content the tools read (for example files on a phone, records in a database or your to-dos) are sent to the provider you choose. Except for “Current time” and “View to-dos”, the model asks you before every tool call. How the provider stores and uses this content is governed by its terms of service and privacy policy.

(2) Before sending, you must make sure you are entitled to provide the content to that provider, especially other people’s personal information obtained in forensic work and other sensitive data. For such data we recommend models that run on your computer (for example Ollama or LM Studio connected as “OpenAI-compatible”).

(3) MCP servers you add may be programs running on your computer or network services. You choose them and are responsible for them.

(4) Conversations and attachments are stored unencrypted in the application data folder on your computer. API keys and sensitive MCP server settings are stored in Windows Credential Manager. Request traces are kept in memory only and are cleared when you exit the Software.

4.4 External MCP is off by default. When it is on, the Software accepts requests that carry a token only on the local address 127.0.0.1 and lets other programs on your computer (for example Claude Code or Codex) call the tools you expose. Content these programs obtain is sent to the services they connect to according to their own settings and is governed by the terms of those programs and services. The token is stored in Windows Credential Manager.

4.5 To-do data is stored in the application data folder on your computer. Reminders are shown as Windows notifications, whose content Windows keeps in the notification center.

4.6 Quick Panel:

(1) When you open the Quick Panel within the set time after copying something (5 seconds by default; you can change this or turn it off in Settings), the Software reads the clipboard once to bring the copied content into the panel, and does not store it otherwise.

(2) Clipboard History is off by default. When it is on, the text, images and file paths you copy are stored encrypted on your computer, and only your current Windows account can decrypt them. Clipboard history is not included in “Back up all data”, and you can clear it at any time.

(3) Content that password managers and similar programs mark as not to be recorded is neither brought into the panel nor recorded in clipboard history.

(4) Text recognition uses the recognition feature built into Windows and runs on your computer; images are not sent anywhere. File search queries Everything, which you install yourself, on your computer. Everything is third-party software and is governed by its own license terms.

(5) To rank frequently used items first, the Software records on your computer which items you open from the Quick Panel, and how often and when you open them. Quick phrases are stored unencrypted; do not use them to store passwords or other sensitive content.

4.7 You can back up your data to a zip file under Settings › Data & Privacy. The backup file is not encrypted and contains conversations, to-dos, settings, drafts and similar content, so keep it safe. Passwords and keys in Windows Credential Manager and the clipboard history are not included. Restoring from a backup replaces your current data; before that, the current data is saved as a separate copy. Restoring does not change anything in Credential Manager. In addition, the conversation and to-do databases are backed up automatically on your computer the first time they are opened each day.

4.8 Settings and drafts are stored in the application data folder on your computer. If you choose “Remember password”, the password is stored in Windows Credential Manager. When uninstalling, you can choose whether to delete the application data folder. Content in Windows Credential Manager is not deleted when you uninstall; delete it in the Software first, or in Windows Credential Manager.

4.9 If a future version needs to collect any information, we will update this agreement first and tell you clearly in the Software.

5. Updates

5.1 We release new versions from time to time, which may fix problems or change or improve features.

5.2 When checking for updates, the Software contacts the release address we designate (currently GitHub) to fetch version information and installers. The operator of that address may log network information such as your IP address. An update is installed only after it passes verification of our digital signature.

5.3 After a new version is released, we do not guarantee that all features of earlier versions keep working. We will try to help when you run into problems, but we do not commit to providing technical support or to resolving issues within any time frame.

6. Installation and removal

6.1 The Software is currently available for Windows only. Obtain the installer from our official release channel and follow the installer’s instructions.

6.2 If you no longer need the Software, uninstall it from Windows Settings › Apps.

7. Intellectual property

7.1 Copyright and other intellectual property rights in the Software, excluding third-party open-source components, belong to xiaoxu123195 and are protected by the laws of the People’s Republic of China and applicable international treaties.

7.2 All rights not expressly granted to you in this agreement are reserved.

8. Restrictions

8.1 Except as permitted by law or with our written permission, you may not:

(1) remove or alter copyright information on the Software or its copies;

(2) reverse engineer, disassemble or decompile the Software, or otherwise attempt to obtain its source code;

(3) modify the Software or create derivative works, or change its functions or behavior by altering or forging its instructions or data at run time;

(4) sell, rent or sublicense the Software;

(5) use the Software for any unlawful purpose.

8.2 Third-party open-source components are used under their own licenses and are not subject to items (2) and (3).

9. Disclaimer and limitation of liability

9.1 The Software is provided free of charge “as is”. It is a preview release and may contain defects or errors. To the maximum extent permitted by law, we make no warranties of any kind, express or implied, including warranties of merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose and non-infringement.

9.2 To the maximum extent permitted by law, we are not liable for any direct or indirect loss arising from the use of or inability to use the Software, including loss or corruption of data, damage to or malfunction of devices, and business interruption. Before collecting, exporting or pushing files, restoring from a backup, or shutting down, restarting, signing out or emptying the Recycle Bin from the Quick Panel, save and back up important data.

9.3 AI-generated content (including answers, translations, organized to-dos and summaries) is produced by the model you choose and may be inaccurate or incomplete. Verify it before use, especially for important purposes such as forensics and reports. To the maximum extent permitted by law, we are not responsible for such content or for any loss caused by relying on it.

9.4 AI providers, MCP servers, programs that call External MCP, and third-party software and services such as Everything and search engines are provided by third parties. We are not responsible for their content, availability, security or charges, and you bear any fees for using them.

9.5 Liability that cannot be excluded or limited under applicable law is not affected by this section.

10. Changes and termination

10.1 We may change this agreement because of changes in law, product updates or business needs. A new agreement is released with a new version, and the main changes are described in the Software or on the release page. By continuing to use the new version, you accept the new agreement.

10.2 If you breach this agreement, we may terminate your license. After termination, you must stop using the Software and delete all copies.

11. Governing law and disputes

11.1 The formation, validity, interpretation, performance and dispute resolution of this agreement are governed by the laws of the People’s Republic of China, excluding its conflict-of-law rules.

11.2 Disputes arising from or relating to this agreement shall first be settled through friendly negotiation. Failing that, either party may bring a lawsuit before the people’s court with jurisdiction at the rights holder’s domicile.

12. Contact

If you have questions or suggestions about this agreement or the Software, or need help, email cherrytump@gmail.com.

Thank you for using Avenlet.
